  "text": "Allergies:\nLisinopril\n\nChief Complaint:\nUrinary retention with urinary tract infection\n\nHistory of Present Illness:\nMr. ___ is a ___ year-old male s/p right hemicolectomy for\nadenocarcinoma on ___ presenting with decreasing ability to\nurinate starting ___ following his discharge.  He reports \nthat\nhe has been doing well since his discharge, however, started\nhaving progressively more difficulty voiding with decreasing\namounts of urine voided.  This afternoon, it progressed to the\npoint where he was severely uncomfortable with suprapubic\ndiscomfort.  He further reports that this afternoon, he started\nto have fevers at home.  He presented to the emergency room this\nafternoon in severe discomfort.  A urinanalysis showed a likely\nurinary tract infection without an elevated white blood cell\ncount.  His discomfort was relieved with the placement of a \nfoley\ncatheter.  His recovery from his operation has been improving \nand\nhe continues to have flatus and normal bowel movements without\nany signs of obstruction. Review of systems was otherwise \nnegative.\n\nBrief Hospital Course:\nThe patient was admitted to the ___ surgery service on \n___ for urinary retention and urinary tract infection with \nsubjective and objective fevers to ___.  His bladder was \nscanned, demonstrating retention of upwards of 700cc, and a \nfoley catheter placed with relief of his suprapubic pain.\n\nUrine analysis demonstrated likely urinary tract infection; the \npatient was given IV ciprofloxacin on HD#1 then switched to oral \nciprofloxacin the next day.\n\nHis foley catheter was removed on HD#2 in the morning and the \npatient was able to void succesfully with minimal post-void \nresiduals.\n\nHe remained afebrile throughout his stay; intake and output were \nclosely monitored.\n\nAt the time of discharge on HD#2, the patient was doing well, \nafebrile with stable vital signs, tolerating a regular diet, \nambulating, voiding without assistance, and pain was well \ncontrolled. He was discharged on Flomax and instructed to \nfollow-up with his PCP regarding its continuation.\n\nDischarge Diagnosis:\nUrinary tract infection, urinary retention",
